  "geometryBasis": "The named main outline and seven mapped component outlines correspond to provincial structural descriptions. Natural Resources Canada’s original bare-earth and first-return elevation crops independently align roof heights and site grade.",
  "sectionBasis": "Provincial engineers record the 94 m Exhibition Building and its long clerestory, the thirteen-storey Fannin tower, the 1997 glass lobby and IMAX, and the original archive wing. Two exact photographer-dedicated CC0 street photographs record the glass entrance, tall limestone-clad piers and low folded archive canopy.",
  "limitations": [
    "Height bands use native roof samples and provincial engineering dimensions. Curtain wall panels, stone tones, stair widths and individual roof fixtures are approximate. The photograph-derived exterior features are matched to the building phase identified in the current operator records.",
    "The scope includes the connected museum masses and the BC Archives wing at the entrance. The independently located carillon and historic precinct houses have their own identities. Interiors, exhibits, temporary signs and display pieces are outside the modeled exterior."
  ],
